  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.5203) clearly outperforms pca_n2000 (0.4849) as an RNA encoder in singleprofile, and image-only (resnet50) is very weak (0.2079), confirming RNA as the dominant signal. The multiprofile dimension is completely untested. This experiment tests whether multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improves upon the best singleprofile RNA result using the strongest encoder (scvi_n200). It isolates the profile/aggregation effect on top of the best encoder, keeping the design simple (no transformer, no multimodal). If multiprofile+avgpool yields a meaningful gain over 0.5203, it justifies further investment in multiprofile variants (transformer, scgpt) in remaining experiments; if not, it redirects budget toward scgpt or multimodal fusion. With 6 experiments left, this is the highest-information single step to determine whether the profile dimension is worth exploiting."
}

